\section{NTEE is not an invariant trait}{

Measured on a 400,000-row sample: \code{ntee_agreement} is \code{unanimous} for 62\%,
\strong{\code{mixed} for 31\%}, and \code{single} for 7\%. Roughly a third of organisations
have been classified inconsistently across vintages. Any schema that stores
one NTEE code per EIN without saying which rule produced it, and without
surfacing that the underlying history disagreed, is presenting a coin flip as
a fact.

Note also that \code{ntee_current} is populated for only 34.7\% of rows while
\code{ntee_most_recent} is populated for 100\%. \code{current} means "currently listed",
not "the current value" - most EINs in the unified file are not in the active
BMF at all.
}

\section{The nteev2 columns carry the known defect}{

They are populated, and they must still be recomputed with
\code{fiscal::get_nteev2()} rather than taken as given. The specialty
double-encoding documented in \code{pfmatch/dev/SCHEDI-ALIAS-FINDINGS.md} §6d is
present: \code{B11} renders as \code{EDU-B11-MS} where the correct value is
\code{EDU-B00-MS}. In NTEEv2 the digits 01-19 encode organisation \emph{type}, not
activity, so the activity slot is \code{B00} and the type is carried by the \code{MS}
suffix - this file emits \code{11} in both slots.

21,983 of the 400,000 sampled rows (5.5\%) carry a 10-19 org-type code and are
affected. Others seen: \code{D11 -> ENV-D11-MS}, \code{S11 -> PSB-S11-MS},
\code{N12 -> HMS-N12-MM}, \code{X19 -> REL-X19-NS}.

Recompute from \code{ntee_code_raw}, not from a cleaned three-character code: the
legacy five-character form carries the \code{B8443 -> B43} rule, which truncation
destroys.
